static.solution:
\kappa(t)=\frac{||\mathbf{r}'(t)\times \mathbf{r}''(t)||}{||\mathbf{r}'(t)||^3}.
We now find
\mathbf{r}'(t) = \langle -5 t^{-2}, 0, 6 \rangle
then
\mathbf{r}''(t) = \langle 10 t^{-3}, 0, 0 \rangle
and so their cross product is
\begin{array}{rcl}
\mathbf{r}'(t)\times \mathbf{r}''(t)
\amp  = \amp  \left|\begin{array}{ccc}\mathbf{i} \amp  \mathbf{j} \amp  \mathbf{k}\\ -5 t^{-2} \amp  0 \amp  6 \\ 10 t^{-3} \amp  0 \amp  0\end{array}\right| \\
\amp  = \amp 
 \left|\begin{array}{cc}0 \amp  6 \\ 0 \amp  0\end{array}\right|\mathbf{i}
-\left|\begin{array}{cc}-5 t^{-2} \amp  6 \\ 10 t^{-3} \amp  0\end{array}\right|\mathbf{j}
+\left|\begin{array}{cc}-5 t^{-2} \amp  0 \\ 10 t^{-3} \amp  0\end{array}\right|\mathbf{k}
 \\
\amp  = \amp  \langle 0, 60 t^{-3}, 0\rangle.
\end{array}
We compute the necessary lengths:
\begin{array}{rcl}
||\mathbf{r}'(t)\times \mathbf{r}''(t)|| \amp  = \amp  60 |t|^{-3} \\
||\mathbf{r}'(t)|| \amp  = \amp  \sqrt{(-5 t^{-2})^2+0^2+6^2}=\sqrt{25 t^{-4}+36}
\end{array}
leaving
\kappa(t)=\frac{60 |t|^{-3}}{(25 t^{-4}+36)^{3/2}}
which can be simplified to
\frac{60 |t|^3}{(25+36 t^4)^{3/2}}.
